- lib/listen/speech/spoken.ts: a spoken text's address in the one player
  (speech:bible/<book>/<chapter>[?in=<bible>], speech:<listen id>?lang=), and
  the language a voice is asked for (the Septuagint's Greek read in the Greek
  of today). playingOf (lib/player/steps.ts) knows a spoken chapter as a
  chapter (Speed, Read at the verse, Share) and a spoken text as a text.
- lib/listen/speech/voices.ts: the phone's voices, asked once and again when
  the sheet opens; their names as a reader can read them (Android's ids by a
  number in their language, a twin listed once); whether the device speaks.
- lib/listen/speech/speak.ts: which voice reads a text (Heart with no engine
  woken where the text has its recording and nothing else is chosen; a gone
  voice said once); a text loaded and read; each voice's pace kept on the
  device (the baton's item 3); a spoken track's end told, for rolling on.
- lib/listen/speech/context.ts: what is playing as the Voice sheet needs it,
  and reading it again in another voice at the verse being read, from the
  player's own words (no fetch).
- lib/readAloud/play.ts listenToChapter and rollOn.ts: Listen on a chapter in
  the reader's voice, the English or a downloaded Bible, the page's own words.
- pageText.ts and sheet.ts: the page's verses handed to Listen; the sheet's state.

